--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Where this software comes from, and what else is in the package
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is the Python port of the Biofermentation Simulation MATLAB App Designer
application (Version 2.2) by Philipp Yuma Iff, which is licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). That application continues the
work of the previous developer of this software, Lena Sophia Kaletsch, who
developed Version 1.3 of the Biofermentation Simulation App (01.03.2024); it
rests in turn on the BIOSIM program conceived by Prof. Dr.-Ing. R. Luttmann.
The software was developed for the laboratory of Bioprocess Automation at the
University of Applied Sciences Hamburg.

The MIT licence above covers this Python implementation. The attribution
required by CC BY 4.0 for the works it derives from is given here and in the
Information tab of the application, and has to travel with any copy.

A packaged build (the single-file executable produced by PyInstaller) also
contains third-party libraries under their own licences, chief among them Qt
by way of PySide6, which is distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public
License version 3. Redistributing such a build carries the obligations of
that licence — see docs/installation.md.
